{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence shows that the RNA encoder is a major performance driver: scvi_n200 improved over pca_n2000 by ~4-7% in the multimodal setting (0.639→0.678 with resnet50; 0.635→0.706 with imagenet_vit_l). However, scgpt has not been tested at all, leaving significant uncertainty about whether a third RNA encoder could outperform scvi_n200. Config_049 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) holds all other dimensions at their empirically best values (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, imagenet_vit_l) and isolates the scgpt-vs-scvi_n200 comparison. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new optimization direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal encoder and lets us redirect budget to other axes (e.g., transformer aggregation or singleprofile trade-offs). Under a limited budget, resolving the RNA encoder question is the highest-value uncertainty to eliminate before fine-tuning secondary choices."
}

